WEBVTT

00:00.790 --> 00:06.930
Zankoku na tenshi no you ni

00:00.790 --> 00:06.930
Just like the cruel angel

00:06.930 --> 00:14.890
Shounen yo shinwa ni nare

00:06.930 --> 00:14.890
Young boy, become a legend

00:18.790 --> 00:22.570
2D4U PRESENTS:

00:22.570 --> 00:25.810
Aoi kaze ga ima

00:22.570 --> 00:25.810
Even though the untested breeze...

00:25.810 --> 00:29.590
mune no doa o tataitemo

00:25.810 --> 00:29.590
...taps at the door to your heart

00:29.590 --> 00:37.270
Watashi dake o tada mitsumete hohoenderu anata

00:29.590 --> 00:37.350
You just look solely at me and smile

00:37.350 --> 00:44.520
Sotto fureru mono motomeru koto ni muchuu de

00:37.360 --> 00:44.520
So intent on seeking out that gentle touch

00:44.520 --> 00:51.860
Unmei sae mada shiranai itaike na hitomi

00:44.520 --> 00:51.860
Such innocent eyes, still ignorant of their destiny

00:51.860 --> 00:55.750
Dakedo itsuka kizuku deshou

00:51.860 --> 00:55.750
But someday, you are sure to realize...

00:55.750 --> 00:58.660
sono senaka ni wa

00:55.750 --> 00:58.660
...that upon your back

00:59.310 --> 01:02.960
Haruka mirai mezasu tame

00:59.310 --> 01:02.960
You have the wings with which to fly...

01:02.960 --> 01:06.610
no hane ga aru koto

01:02.960 --> 01:06.770
...towards the distant future

01:06.770 --> 01:10.750
Zankoku na tenshi no teeze

01:06.790 --> 01:10.750
The cruel angel's thesis

01:10.750 --> 01:14.430
Madobe kara yagate tobidatsu

01:10.750 --> 01:14.430
Soon, you will take flight from the windowsill

01:14.430 --> 01:18.260
Hotobashiru atsui patosu de

01:14.430 --> 01:18.260
With your torrent of ardent pathos

01:18.260 --> 01:21.760
Omoide o uragiru nara

01:18.260 --> 01:21.760
If you are to betray our memories

01:21.760 --> 01:25.540
Kono sora o daite kagayaku

01:21.760 --> 01:25.540
You, who embrace these heavens and shine

01:25.540 --> 01:29.570
Shounen yo shinwa ni nare

01:25.540 --> 01:29.570
Young boy, become a legend

01:31.030 --> 01:33.940
Hello, I'm not home right now.

01:33.940 --> 01:36.830
Please leave your message after the beep.

01:40.500 --> 01:42.840
My last job...

01:43.500 --> 01:45.580
The red is as if it's for the color of blood.

01:45.620 --> 01:48.540
EPISODE 21
NERV IS BORN

01:48.540 --> 01:51.130
Abducted?! The Vice Commander?

01:51.130 --> 01:53.210
It happened two hours ago.

01:53.210 --> 01:56.380
He was last seen in District 8 on the west side.

01:56.380 --> 01:58.260
That's within our compound!

01:58.260 --> 02:00.550
What was your Intelligence Department doing?!

02:00.550 --> 02:03.810
There's an insider who leaked information
and instigated this.

02:03.810 --> 02:05.850
He was able to get the better of us.

02:05.850 --> 02:08.560
Someone who can pull the wool over
the eyes of Intelligence Division 2?

02:08.560 --> 02:10.230
It can't be!

02:10.230 --> 02:13.980
Ryoji Kaji is the man believed to be
the mastermind behind this.

02:13.980 --> 02:16.650
And that's why you're here.

02:16.650 --> 02:18.950
We appreciate your quick understanding.

02:18.950 --> 02:20.910
As a member of the same organization,

02:20.910 --> 02:23.780
it is regrettable that we must suspect
the Chief of Operations,

02:23.780 --> 02:25.590
but this is pan of our job.

02:25.590 --> 02:28.040
Considering the history between me and him,

02:28.040 --> 02:30.080
it seems like the logical step to take.

02:30.080 --> 02:31.750
Thank you for your cooperation.

02:31.750 --> 02:33.340
Take her away.

02:34.350 --> 02:36.420
It has been a while, Chairman Kiel.

02:36.420 --> 02:39.000
This is quite a rude welcome.

02:39.000 --> 02:41.810
I need not apologize to you for the impropriety.

02:42.140 --> 02:45.890
This is a necessary procedure in order
to speak with you at leisure.

02:46.140 --> 02:47.930
You certainly haven't changed.

02:47.930 --> 02:50.480
Does my convenience mean nothing then?

02:50.480 --> 02:53.270
The problem being discussed
is an urgent matter.

02:53.270 --> 02:54.900
It was unavoidable.

02:54.900 --> 02:56.530
Please understand.

02:56.780 --> 02:59.990
So, it's Seele and not the Committee.

02:59.990 --> 03:03.320
We have no intention of creating a new god.

03:03.320 --> 03:06.890
We would like your cooperation,
Professor Fuyutsuki.

03:06.890 --> 03:09.920
Professor Fuyutsuki...

03:10.260 --> 03:11.290
Professor! Professor Fuyutsuki!

03:11.290 --> 03:12.750
YEAR 1999, KYOTO

03:11.290 --> 03:12.750
Professor! Professor Fuyutsuki!

03:13.720 --> 03:16.460
Oh, it's you two.

03:16.460 --> 03:19.170
You wanna join us for some beer in Kamogawa?

03:19.170 --> 03:20.380
Again?

03:20.380 --> 03:23.970
Ryoko and the others are saying
they'll go if you go.

03:23.970 --> 03:27.140
Our professor was also saying you should
show up once in a while.

03:27.140 --> 03:29.110
Sure, all right.

03:29.900 --> 03:32.940
It's good to go out and have
a drink every so often.

03:32.940 --> 03:34.020
Yes, Sir.

03:34.020 --> 03:35.650
You excel at your work,

03:35.650 --> 03:39.150
but you don't take socializing seriously
and that's not good.

03:39.150 --> 03:40.650
I'm sure you're right.

03:40.650 --> 03:42.530
By the way, Fuyutsuki,

03:42.530 --> 03:47.120
there's a bioengineering student
who submitted an interesting paper.

03:47.120 --> 03:50.160
The student's name is Ikari. Do you know her?

03:50.160 --> 03:52.510
Ikari? No, I don't.

03:52.510 --> 03:56.210
I told her about you and she said
she was interested in meeting you.

03:56.210 --> 03:59.800
She'll probably contact you eventually,
so take care of things, will you?

03:59.800 --> 04:02.260
Ikari, was it? All right.

04:02.260 --> 04:03.800
Metaphysical Biology Research Room 1 Fuyutsuki

04:04.120 --> 04:06.350
I read your paper.

04:06.350 --> 04:09.770
I found a couple of things questionable,
but it was a stimulating paper.

04:09.770 --> 04:11.350
Thank you very much.

04:11.350 --> 04:13.810
Yui Ikari, wasn't it?

04:13.810 --> 04:14.900
Yes.

04:14.900 --> 04:16.770
What are your plans for the future?

04:16.770 --> 04:18.020
Are you going to find work?

04:18.020 --> 04:21.030
Or do you intend to join the research lab here?

04:21.030 --> 04:23.400
I haven't thought that far ahead yet.

04:23.400 --> 04:26.910
And besides, aren't you forgetting a third option?

04:26.910 --> 04:30.080
I'm also considering a domestic life.

04:30.080 --> 04:32.670
Of course, that's only if I can find someone nice.

04:32.960 --> 04:34.250
BACK IN THE YEAR 2015

04:34.300 --> 04:37.420
With an S2 engine on board,

04:37.420 --> 04:41.380
Evangelion Unit 01 has become
an absolute being!

04:41.380 --> 04:45.090
We have no use for an actualized god.

04:45.090 --> 04:47.430
We must not create a god.

04:47.430 --> 04:50.860
We cannot allow that man to create a god.

04:50.860 --> 04:54.870
Gendo Ikari, is he a man that can be trusted?

04:54.870 --> 04:57.980
Gendo Rokubungi? I've heard of him.

04:58.020 --> 05:00.820
BACK IN THE YEAR 1999

04:58.730 --> 05:01.180
No, I've never met him,

05:01.180 --> 05:04.190
but there's always some rumor
going around about him.

05:02.570 --> 05:04.190
Kyoto Prefecture Police Department

05:04.650 --> 05:08.340
What? He asked to be released
into my custody?

05:08.340 --> 05:10.080
No, I'll come.

05:10.080 --> 05:12.340
When should I come over there?

05:12.750 --> 05:16.450
I heard about you from a certain person,

05:16.450 --> 05:19.050
so I wanted to meet you.

05:19.590 --> 05:23.010
You're a rather coarse man,
to get into a drunken brawl.

05:23.010 --> 05:25.970
There was no time to talk.
They just picked a fight with me.

05:26.130 --> 05:28.260
I'm not very good at being liked,

05:28.260 --> 05:30.730
but I am used to being treated coldly.

05:31.730 --> 05:34.450
Well, it's none of my business anyway.

05:34.450 --> 05:36.100
Professor Fuyutsuki,

05:36.100 --> 05:39.820
you seem to be exactly the person
I expected you to be.

05:40.230 --> 05:44.880
Yes, my first impression of him was of distaste.

05:44.880 --> 05:49.660
And back then, seasons and autumn
still existed in this country.

05:49.660 --> 05:50.990
Are you serious?

05:50.990 --> 05:54.750
Yes, I am seeing Mr. Rokubungi.

05:54.750 --> 05:58.630
When I heard that, I wasn't able
to hide my surprise.

05:59.840 --> 06:02.710
I never would have thought you would
share your time with him.

06:02.710 --> 06:07.430
Oh, but Professor Fuyutsuki,
he's quite a sweet person.

06:07.430 --> 06:09.430
It's just that no one knows it.

06:09.430 --> 06:12.550
Maybe it's more blissful not to know.

06:12.550 --> 06:15.680
Did I inconvenience you by
introducing you to him?

06:15.680 --> 06:20.400
No, I'll admit that he's an interesting man,
though I can't get to like him.

06:21.530 --> 06:26.240
But within our circle, the common opinion
was that he had approached Yui

06:26.240 --> 06:29.440
for her talent and for
the organization backing her.

06:29.440 --> 06:34.160
Later, I would hear rumors that this
organization was called Seele.

06:34.370 --> 06:35.830
YEAR 2000, ANTARCTICA

06:36.190 --> 06:38.000
The Second Impact.

06:38.000 --> 06:41.000
That tragedy occurred in the final year
of the 20th century.

06:41.040 --> 06:48.510
YEAR 2001

06:41.500 --> 06:45.800
And the first year of
the 21st century was pure hell.

06:45.800 --> 06:48.420
There is no other word to describe that year.

06:48.550 --> 06:49.430
YEAR 2002

06:52.230 --> 06:55.290
To think this was once a continent of ice...

06:55.290 --> 06:57.270
There's no trace of it left.

06:57.270 --> 06:59.110
Professor Fuyutsuki...

06:59.440 --> 07:00.730
You?

07:00.730 --> 07:02.530
I'm surprised you survived.

07:02.530 --> 07:06.410
I'd heard that you were a member
of the Katsuragi Research Team.

07:06.410 --> 07:09.610
Luckily, I had returned to Japan
the day before the incident,

07:09.610 --> 07:11.530
so I was able to escape the tragedy.

07:11.530 --> 07:13.000
I see.

07:13.000 --> 07:14.580
Rokubungi, you...

07:14.580 --> 07:17.340
Excuse me, I have a different name now.

07:18.840 --> 07:21.210
A postcard? Not a business card?

07:21.210 --> 07:22.620
We're Married

07:21.210 --> 07:22.620
Gendo & Yui
Ikari

07:21.210 --> 07:22.620
It has been
a long time.
Are you doing well?

07:23.380 --> 07:26.040
Ikari? Gendo Ikari...

07:26.040 --> 07:29.510
My wife has been nagging me to get
this to you, Professor Fuyutsuki.

07:29.510 --> 07:31.590
She seems to be a fan of yours.

07:31.590 --> 07:32.760
I'm honored.

07:32.760 --> 07:37.010
Gendo & Yui
Ikari

07:32.760 --> 07:37.010
It has been
a long time.
Are you doing well?

07:33.590 --> 07:35.220
How is Yui doing?

07:35.220 --> 07:37.380
Isn't she participating in this expedition?

07:37.380 --> 07:41.650
Yui wanted to come, but we
have a child now, so...

07:42.520 --> 07:51.200
SAFETY FIRST

07:43.100 --> 07:46.190
Your organization... Seele, was it?

07:46.190 --> 07:48.070
I've heard nothing but bad things about it.

07:48.070 --> 07:51.670
I can't approve of forcibly
pinning down the board of directors.

07:51.670 --> 07:53.990
You're fastidious as ever.

07:53.990 --> 07:57.280
No clean organization can survive
in this day and age anymore.

07:57.280 --> 08:00.250
The official investigation of the Second Impact...

08:00.250 --> 08:03.420
If the investigation team consisted
only of Seele people,

08:03.420 --> 08:05.730
you would run into all sons of issues later.

08:05.730 --> 08:08.720
We're just a makeshift solution
to avoid that, aren't we?

08:10.550 --> 08:11.510
YEAR 2015

08:11.550 --> 08:13.800
NERV HEADQUARTERS - ISOLATION FACILITY 4

08:13.980 --> 08:16.550
I still don't handle dark places very well.

08:16.550 --> 08:18.610
All the bad memories come flooding back.

08:19.230 --> 08:20.520
Who is she?

08:20.520 --> 08:23.020
She's the sole survivor of the original expedition.

08:23.060 --> 08:24.020
YEAR 2002

08:24.060 --> 08:27.020
SOUTH POLE INVESTIGATION SHIP - ISOLATION FACILITY 2

08:24.060 --> 08:26.230
Her name is Misato Katsuragi.

08:26.230 --> 08:28.900
Katsuragi? She's Dr. Katsuragi's daughter?

08:29.120 --> 08:32.790
Yes, she hasn't spoken for
almost two years now.

08:32.790 --> 08:34.150
That's terrible.

08:34.150 --> 08:36.280
It attests to the hell that she witnessed.

08:36.280 --> 08:37.950
Her physical injuries have healed,

08:37.950 --> 08:40.790
but psychological wounds do not heal so easily.

08:41.420 --> 08:42.500
I suppose so.

08:42.500 --> 08:45.710
SAFETY FIRST

08:43.160 --> 08:45.710
We can't conclude our findings
for our investigation lightly either.

08:45.960 --> 08:49.040
This giant of light...
This incident is full of mysteries.

08:49.040 --> 08:55.880
United Nations Moves Headquarters to Japan
In Five Years, Candidate is New Tokyo-2
Second Impact Caused by a Massive Meteor
Impossible to Predict or Avoid
Probability of Once in Every Several
Hundred Million Years
Official United Nations Statement
At 20-30% of the Speed of Light

08:49.460 --> 08:51.880
Soon after, the United Nations issued an official statement

08:51.880 --> 08:55.880
stating that the Second Impact was caused by a massive meteor.

08:55.880 --> 08:58.800
But from where I stood, I could see

08:58.800 --> 09:02.140
that the information had been
blatantly massaged.

09:02.140 --> 09:07.310
Behind all this was Seele and hints that
a man named Kiel was involved.

09:07.310 --> 09:11.430
And it made me want to learn the
dark truth of that incident.

09:11.730 --> 09:12.940
YEAR 2003, HAKONE

09:11.730 --> 09:15.150
Even if that might eventually lead me to the name of Yui Ikari.

09:12.990 --> 09:15.150
UNITED NATIONS ARTIFICIAL EVOLUTION LABORATORY

09:15.150 --> 09:16.950
{DIRECTOR'S OFFICE

09:16.950 --> 09:20.000
Why do you hide the existence
of the giant of light?!

09:20.460 --> 09:24.290
You guys knew about the
Second Impact, didn't you?

09:24.290 --> 09:24.830
That it would happen on that day?

09:24.830 --> 09:26.250
That it would happen on that day?

09:24.910 --> 09:27.290
LABORATORY DIRECTOR GENDO IKARI

09:27.770 --> 09:31.920
You said you were lucky enough
to get out the day before.

09:32.100 --> 09:35.970
Was it also luck that you took
all your research with you?!

09:37.680 --> 09:41.560
I am surprised that this material
escaped destruction.

09:41.560 --> 09:44.820
I did a thorough investigation of your assets.

09:45.230 --> 09:47.850
I'm sure raising a child is expensive,

09:47.850 --> 09:50.810
but isn't the amount rather large
for you to have privately?

09:50.810 --> 09:52.900
You impress me, Professor Fuyutsuki.

09:52.900 --> 09:55.490
Why not transfer to the department
of economics?

09:55.490 --> 09:58.820
I'm going to go public about Seele
and the Dead Sea Scrolls

09:58.820 --> 10:01.170
being secretly behind the Second Impact.

10:01.170 --> 10:04.160
I have no intention of letting the people
who caused that get away with it!

10:04.160 --> 10:05.450
Feel free.

10:05.450 --> 10:08.420
But before you do, there is something
I would like to show you.

10:10.840 --> 10:12.960
We're going down quite a ways.

10:12.960 --> 10:14.500
Does it worry you?

10:14.500 --> 10:15.720
Somewhat.

10:17.770 --> 10:18.880
What is this?

10:18.880 --> 10:22.140
A cavern left behind by someone,
who was not us.

10:22.140 --> 10:24.930
Though eighty-nine percent of it is buried.

10:24.930 --> 10:28.440
An underground cavern that was originally
a neat spherical shape...

10:28.440 --> 10:32.820
All the resources mankind has to offer
are being poured into that facility.

10:39.200 --> 10:41.320
Oh, Professor Fuyutsuki.

10:41.710 --> 10:43.910
Akagi, you too?

10:43.910 --> 10:47.160
Yes, this is the best place to research

10:47.160 --> 10:50.050
the fundamental theories for the
bio-computers of the future.

10:50.050 --> 10:51.500
I see.

10:51.500 --> 10:53.590
I intend to name it Magi.

10:53.590 --> 10:56.890
Magi? After the three wise men from the East?

10:56.890 --> 10:59.040
Is this what you wanted to show me?

10:59.040 --> 11:01.890
No, this way, please.

11:01.890 --> 11:04.100
Ritsuko, I'll be right back.

11:06.940 --> 11:08.430
What is this?

11:08.430 --> 11:10.020
Is this that giant?!

11:10.020 --> 11:13.400
Here at Gehirn, we call that giant Adam.

11:13.400 --> 11:14.940
But this is not it.

11:14.940 --> 11:17.120
It is not the original.

11:18.080 --> 11:19.030
Then...

11:19.030 --> 11:23.200
Yes, it is an Eva, made from Adam by man.

11:23.200 --> 11:24.450
An Eva?!

11:24.450 --> 11:26.830
This is the Adam Revival Project,

11:26.830 --> 11:29.200
generally known as Project E,
and this is our mockup,

11:29.200 --> 11:31.130
<i>Eva Unit 00.</i>

11:31.130 --> 11:33.290
A Prototype for a god?!

11:33.290 --> 11:34.540
Fuyutsuki,

11:34.540 --> 11:38.560
work with me to create a new era
in the history of mankind.

11:44.140 --> 11:45.100
YEAR 2015

11:46.190 --> 11:48.100
Excuse me, Ma'am?

11:48.100 --> 11:51.810
Oh, I'm sorry. Let's hurry up and retest Rei.

11:51.810 --> 11:54.580
I haven't seen Miss Katsuragi around today.

11:54.580 --> 11:56.070
You're right.

11:56.570 --> 11:57.900
Miss Katsuragi?

11:57.900 --> 12:00.280
Right! Misato Katsuragi! Nice to meet you!

12:00.280 --> 12:02.240
YEAR 2005
NEW TOKYO-2, NAGANO PREFECTURE

12:01.740 --> 12:02.280
Mother,

12:02.320 --> 12:05.740
2ND TOKYO UNIVERSITY, SCHOOL GROUNDS

12:03.070 --> 12:05.740
I met a girl named Katsuragi the other day.

12:05.740 --> 12:08.700
Other people will only look at me from afar,

12:08.700 --> 12:12.210
and each time, I am reminded of
the weight your name carries,

12:12.210 --> 12:16.170
but this girl has no reservation
towards me for some reason.

12:16.930 --> 12:20.720
I am told that she is the sole survivor
of that expedition.

12:20.720 --> 12:23.050
She was apparently aphasic for a time,

12:23.050 --> 12:27.050
but now, she chatters away a mile a minute
as if to make up for lost time.

12:27.810 --> 12:32.110
Ritchan, I am still burrowed underground,
the same as always.

12:32.110 --> 12:34.850
I've grown tired of the lunches they provide.

12:34.850 --> 12:38.020
On the surface, they have apparently begun
working on the plans for New Tokyo-S

12:38.020 --> 12:40.330
in accordance with the Second
Capital Transfer Project.

12:40.830 --> 12:43.490
Lately, Misato hadn't been showing up
at the university,

12:43.490 --> 12:46.420
and when I finally got her to tell me why,
it was so idiotic.

12:46.420 --> 12:50.660
Apparently, she had been sleeping with
her boyfriend at her apartment,

12:50.660 --> 12:52.950
for an entire week!

12:52.950 --> 12:55.760
I feel like I have seen an unexpected side of her.

12:56.130 --> 12:58.210
She introduced him to me today.

12:58.210 --> 12:59.630
He's good-looking,

12:59.630 --> 13:02.640
but I just cannot get to like his frivolous attitude.

13:03.390 --> 13:07.010
As I recall, you have never been
good around boys, Ritchan.

13:07.010 --> 13:09.430
In the end, being raised only by a woman...

13:09.430 --> 13:12.850
No, I'm sorry. I have left you to your
own devices for so long.

13:13.020 --> 13:16.650
It's awful of me to act like a mother
only when it's convenient.

13:18.240 --> 13:19.400
A mother...

13:19.440 --> 13:20.400
YEAR 2004

13:20.480 --> 13:21.900
HAKONE - UNDERGROUND LABORATORY 2

13:21.900 --> 13:24.690
LCL electrified. Pressure at plus zero point two.

13:24.690 --> 13:26.740
No destrudo readings detected in transmissions.

13:26.740 --> 13:28.450
<i>Para-base is stable.</i>

13:26.950 --> 13:29.070
What is this child doing here?

13:29.070 --> 13:31.370
He's Director Ikari's son.

13:31.370 --> 13:35.530
Ikari, this is not a nursery school.
Today is a crucial day!

13:35.530 --> 13:39.130
I'm sorry, Professor Fuyutsuki.
I'm the one who brought him.

13:39.130 --> 13:42.460
Yui, this is your experiment today.

13:42.460 --> 13:43.920
That's why.

13:43.920 --> 13:47.280
I want to show my child the bright future.

13:47.280 --> 13:50.390
Those were Ms. Yui's final words.

13:50.390 --> 13:54.400
The irregular circumstances erased her
from this world.

13:54.770 --> 13:58.040
Exactly as I had wished.

13:58.040 --> 14:01.170
I am such a horrible woman.

14:01.170 --> 14:04.940
Ritchan, Director Ikari changed after that day.

14:05.540 --> 14:08.060
Where have you been for the past week?

14:08.060 --> 14:10.950
You're allowed to grieve, but you
need to be aware

14:10.950 --> 14:13.580
that you are responsible for
more than yourself now.

14:13.580 --> 14:14.950
I know.

14:14.950 --> 14:19.160
Fuyutsuki, I am going to recommend
a new project starting today.

14:19.160 --> 14:21.750
I have already proposed it to Chairman Kiel.

14:21.750 --> 14:23.550
You're not going to...

14:23.550 --> 14:24.670
That's right.

14:24.670 --> 14:27.800
The path to godhood that none have
ever succeeded in before.

14:27.800 --> 14:29.800
The Human Instrumentality Project.

14:29.930 --> 14:30.890
YEAR 2008

14:31.440 --> 14:32.930
Mother,

14:32.930 --> 14:35.520
congratulations on the completion of
the fundamental theory of Magi.

14:35.520 --> 14:37.680
This is not exactly a gift to celebrate it with,

14:37.680 --> 14:41.190
but my formal admission into Gehirn
has been unofficially approved.

14:41.190 --> 14:44.280
I will be working on Project E
starting next month.

14:49.160 --> 14:51.000
Who's there?

14:53.000 --> 14:55.540
Technology Development Department,
Ritsuko Akagi.

14:55.540 --> 14:57.170
Here's my ID.

14:57.170 --> 14:59.160
I heard the command center
had been completed,

14:59.160 --> 15:02.130
so I came to see it, but this place is a maze.

15:02.130 --> 15:06.210
If you want the command center,
the Director and Dr. Akagi are there.

15:08.060 --> 15:10.180
Are you really sure?

15:10.180 --> 15:13.220
Yes, I have no regrets concerning my work.

15:13.220 --> 15:16.610
Liar! You just can't forget about Ms. Yui, right?

15:18.110 --> 15:20.570
But I don't mind.

15:29.240 --> 15:30.200
YEAR 2010

15:30.200 --> 15:31.610
GEOFRONT ARTIFICIAL CANOPY

15:31.700 --> 15:33.660
LOWER LEVEL 2 DIRECT SUPPORT AREA (FUTURE LOCATION)

15:35.630 --> 15:38.170
That's the headquarters for Gehirn.

15:39.380 --> 15:41.660
Good morning, Director.

15:41.660 --> 15:43.580
Did you bring your child today?

15:43.580 --> 15:46.460
Oh, but you have a son, if I'm not mistaken.

15:46.460 --> 15:48.050
This isn't Shinji.

15:48.050 --> 15:50.590
I'm taking care of a friend's daughter.

15:50.590 --> 15:52.720
Her name is Rei Ayanami.

15:52.720 --> 15:54.850
Hello, Rei.

15:55.690 --> 15:58.830
This girl reminds me of someone...

15:58.830 --> 16:00.650
Ms. Yui?

16:01.360 --> 16:05.100
All files concerning Rei Ayanami
have been erased already?

16:05.100 --> 16:06.940
It's blank.

16:06.940 --> 16:07.860
What does this mean?

16:07.860 --> 16:10.070
COMPLETED

16:10.070 --> 16:14.790
Magi Casper, Magi Balthasar,
and Magi Melchior.

16:15.370 --> 16:17.370
The Magi are the three pans
that make up who I am.

16:17.370 --> 16:22.710
The scientist in me, the mother in me,
and the woman in me.

16:23.130 --> 16:25.580
And those three elements will be in
constant conflict with one another.

16:25.580 --> 16:27.730
The three pans of you...

16:27.730 --> 16:30.670
The only thing left is to power it up, right?

16:31.890 --> 16:34.090
I'm going to go home early today.

16:34.090 --> 16:35.550
Misato's coming back.

16:35.550 --> 16:38.850
That's right, I didn't know she
was a member of Gehirn.

16:38.850 --> 16:40.270
I believe she's in Germany?

16:40.270 --> 16:42.480
Yes, she's serving in Branch 3.

16:42.480 --> 16:44.850
Then I suppose it's a long-distance relationship.

16:44.850 --> 16:46.270
I heard they broke up.

16:46.270 --> 16:49.440
Oh, and they looked so good together too.

16:49.440 --> 16:51.480
You can never tell with a man and a woman,

16:51.480 --> 16:53.110
because it's not logical.

16:53.110 --> 16:56.000
That cool attitude of yours
certainly hasn't changed.

16:56.000 --> 16:59.210
You're going to let your own
happiness slip away.

16:59.540 --> 17:02.540
Happiness is even harder to define.

17:02.540 --> 17:05.870
Well, it's been a longtime since
I've gone drinking.

17:05.870 --> 17:07.130
Goodnight.

17:07.130 --> 17:08.720
Goodnight.

17:21.610 --> 17:23.850
Did you want something, Rei?

17:23.850 --> 17:25.480
I got lost.

17:25.480 --> 17:29.570
Oh, really? Then you want to
leave here with me?

17:30.200 --> 17:31.480
That's okay.

17:31.480 --> 17:33.820
But you won't be able to get home
by yourself, right?

17:33.820 --> 17:36.540
That's none of your business, you old hag.

17:37.460 --> 17:38.660
What?

17:38.660 --> 17:42.010
I can go home by myself,
so leave me alone, you old hag.

17:42.010 --> 17:45.290
It's not nice to call someone an old hag.

17:45.290 --> 17:47.460
But you are an old hag, aren't you?

17:47.460 --> 17:51.170
I'm going to get mad. You need
a good scolding from Director Ikari.

17:51.170 --> 17:54.010
That's what the Director calls you.

17:54.010 --> 17:54.840
That...

17:54.840 --> 17:56.420
He says, “That old hag is pushy,”

17:56.420 --> 17:59.020
or that he, “doesn't need that old hag anymore.”

17:59.020 --> 18:00.640
He says, “That old hag is pushy,”

18:00.640 --> 18:03.010
or that he, “doesn't need that old hag anymore.”

18:03.680 --> 18:05.930
He doesn't need that old hag anymore.

18:05.930 --> 18:10.530
It's what the Director calls you.

18:16.410 --> 18:18.200
You're nothing but a...

18:18.200 --> 18:20.780
It doesn't matter if you die,
you can always be replaced.

18:20.780 --> 18:22.440
Rei...

18:22.440 --> 18:24.630
The same as me.

18:32.710 --> 18:36.590
The Human Instrumentality Project Committee,
chaired by Kiel Lorenz,

18:36.590 --> 18:39.760
dissolved the research organization,
Gehirn, the next day.

18:39.760 --> 18:41.850
And they formed the special duty
organization, Nerv,

18:41.850 --> 18:44.350
as the organization that would
carry out all projects.

18:44.350 --> 18:48.270
All of us were moved directly into Nerv,

18:48.270 --> 18:53.570
with the exception of one, Dr. Akagi,
the remarkable creator of the Magi System.

18:53.610 --> 18:54.570
YEAR 2015

18:59.530 --> 19:00.990
Oh, it's you.

19:00.990 --> 19:02.490
Long time no see.

19:02.490 --> 19:05.600
I've put the guards outside to sleep for a while.

19:05.600 --> 19:08.960
This will cost you your life.

19:08.960 --> 19:11.330
I just want to get closer to the truth

19:11.330 --> 19:13.220
within myself.

19:15.210 --> 19:17.930
Thank you very much for your cooperation.

19:18.890 --> 19:20.380
Is it over?

19:20.380 --> 19:23.350
Yes, the problem has been resolved, so...

19:24.560 --> 19:26.310
I see.

19:27.320 --> 19:28.600
What about him?

19:28.600 --> 19:30.190
I do not know.

19:42.710 --> 19:45.500
Hey, you're late.

19:50.210 --> 19:51.840
I'm home.

20:15.360 --> 20:16.810
Play

20:15.360 --> 20:16.810
Messages

20:25.870 --> 20:29.290
Play

20:32.920 --> 20:35.440
Katsuragi, it's me.

20:35.440 --> 20:37.880
I've probably put you through a lot of trouble

20:37.880 --> 20:40.820
by the time you're listening to this.

20:40.820 --> 20:42.470
I'm sorry.

20:42.470 --> 20:45.140
Tell Ritchan I said I'm sorry too.

20:45.140 --> 20:47.640
Also, since I've troubled you so much anyway,

20:47.640 --> 20:50.060
there's this flower I've been growing...

20:50.060 --> 20:52.860
It'd make me happy if you'd water it for me.

20:53.320 --> 20:55.780
Shinji knows where it is.

20:56.320 --> 21:00.120
Katsuragi, the truth is with you.

21:00.120 --> 21:02.660
Go forward without any hesitation.

21:03.160 --> 21:06.540
If I ever get to see you again,

21:06.540 --> 21:09.680
I'll say the words I wasn't able
to say eight years ago.

21:09.680 --> 21:11.540
Bye.

21:11.540 --> 21:14.460
Message recorded at 12:02pm.

21:17.010 --> 21:18.790
Jerk...

21:19.550 --> 21:23.010
You're really such a jerk...

21:45.080 --> 21:49.620
Right then, all I could do was
run away from Misato.

21:50.210 --> 21:54.710
There was nothing I could do or say.
I was a child.

21:56.090 --> 21:57.420
It made me realize that.

21:57.460 --> 22:00.630
TO BE CONTINUED

23:06.070 --> 23:06.940
PREVIEW

23:06.940 --> 23:10.360
Asuka falls into a psychological pitfall
due to having lost to Shinji.

23:10.360 --> 23:12.740
Furthermore, the psychological attack
from an Angel

23:12.740 --> 23:14.780
delivers the finishing blow to Asuka's mind.

23:14.780 --> 23:18.000
Shinji is unable to offer her
any words of comfort.

23:18.000 --> 23:20.540
Next time, "At Least, Be Human"

23:18.370 --> 23:21.080
AT LEAST, BE HUMAN
